    oe:aboutDisease oed:sepsis ;
    oe:answerText "Interventions to induce lasting human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) remission are needed to obviate the requirement for lifelong antiretroviral therapy. Durable post-intervention control (PIC) of viraemia has been achieved in a subset of people following administration of broadly neutralizing anti-HIV-1 antibodies (bNAb) and analytical interruption of treatment."^^xsd:string ;
